-- title:
--   Supersingular charts as μ_{q+1}-quotients of the Drinfeld curve
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$, and write $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\kappa$-algebra `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,M'$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places, i.e. the rational affine geometric places $w$ with $w$-value of the generator `jGeomGen` in `ssJSet q κ`. Assume `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series, is contained in `fieldBar q M'`, the corresponding base change for level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of the unit reduction map. Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` along $A$ with values in `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` which, by hypothesis, is coefficientwise reduction: every Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ that lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0$'s integers and has residue the coefficientwise reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Fix $s\in W$, a field $Fbar$ over $\kappa$ and a component chart $C$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $A$ with values in $Fbar$, and assume: some element of $Fbar$ is transcendental over $\kappa$; $C$ lies over $s$ through $R_0$, in the sense that for $f$ in $R_0$'s integers having non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` where the image of $j_q$ has non-negative order and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation ring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $C$'s integers with $C$-residue the image in $Fbar$ of the value at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$; and the integers of $C$ are unchanged by pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$. Assume further that $\kappa$ is an $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra and that the Drinfeld coordinate ring `CoordRing q κ` is a domain. Then there is a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity in $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ with $|C_s| = 2\,$`placeWidthChar q M' s` and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism between $Fbar$ and [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ C_s`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32), the fixed field in the Drinfeld function field over $\kappa$ of the group generated by the scalar action of $C_s$.
--
--   This is the identification step in the analysis of the supersingular components of the semistable reduction at $q$ of the modular curve of level $K(q)K_0(M')$: a level-stable component chart lying over a supersingular point $s$ has reduced function field the fixed field of a group of order twice the width of $s$ acting by scalars on the Drinfeld curve $xy^q-x^qy=1$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.two_mul_placeWidthChar_mul_genusFF_add_of_chart_over`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.two_mul_placeWidthChar_mul_genusFF_add_of_chart_over), where it is combined with Riemann–Hurwitz for the scalar action to compute the genus of the component.
